{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgk2rfTHPoZ5rBU71fCVa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CsJUntxCjNxZaCfP37jeSX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/sim/bot.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  // Anything that needs two hands comes first, wherever it is.\"\"\",\"\"\"  if (sim.context) return nextTask(sim, seat, sim.context);\n  // Anything that needs two hands comes first, wherever it is.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"kenney-furniture\" LIBRARY.md | head -5; awk '/kenney-furniture/{f=1} f&&/^\\|/' LIBRARY.md | head -5; node -e \"\nconst lib=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('library.json','utf8'));\nconst items=(lib.models||lib).filter? (lib.models||lib):Object.values(lib);\nconst f=items.filter(i=>(i.pack||'').includes('furniture'));\nconsole.log(f.length, f.map(i=>i.id.replace('kenney-furniture/','')).join(' '));\n\"; sed -n 3022,3036p API.md; sed -n 2884,2900p API.md; sed -n 3597,3612p API.md; sed -n 4580,4582p API.md; grep -n \"interface PrecipitationOptions\" -A10 API.md | head -14; grep -n \"^### class CameraRig\" -A26 API.md | sed -n 1,30p","description":"Fix bot context, list furniture pack and API details"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5886,"cache_read_input_tokens":270585,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5886},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"597d3a1c-db2a-4749-a8fd-5a8ff36f0d78","uuid":"44896640-e220-4042-b670-3537d17c8459","timestamp":"2026-11-05T15:39:57.663Z","request_id":"req_011Cgk2rf3iEx6HzkJEsLCXg","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CsJUntxCjNxZaCfP37jeSX":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/sim/bot.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  // Anything that needs two hands comes first, wherever it is.\"\"\",\"\"\"  if (sim.context) return nextTask(sim, seat, sim.context);\n  // Anything that needs two hands comes first, wherever it is.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"kenney-furniture\" LIBRARY.md | head -5; awk '/kenney-furniture/{f=1} f&&/^\\|/' LIBRARY.md | head -5; node -e \"\nconst lib=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('library.json','utf8'));\nconst items=(lib.models||lib).filter? (lib.models||lib):Object.values(lib);\nconst f=items.filter(i=>(i.pack||'').includes('furniture'));\nconsole.log(f.length, f.map(i=>i.id.replace('kenney-furniture/','')).join(' '));\n\"; sed -n 3022,3036p API.md; sed -n 2884,2900p API.md; sed -n 3597,3612p API.md; sed -n 4580,4582p API.md; grep -n \"interface PrecipitationOptions\" -A10 API.md | head -14; grep -n \"^### class CameraRig\" -A26 API.md | sed -n 1,30p","description":"Fix bot context, list furniture pack and API details"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CsJUntxCjNxZaCfP37jeSX","type":"tool_result","content":"435:### kenney-furniture: Kenney Furniture Kit 2.0\n437:140 models, 0 textures, CC0-1.0 by Kenney (https://kenney.nl/assets/furniture-kit). Load it: `const kit = await loadPack('packs/kenney-furniture.json')`, then `buildModel(id, { catalog: kit })`.\n441:| `kenney-furniture/bathroom-cabinet` | 0.46 × 0.78 × 0.26 |  | wood sand, metal mist, woodDark orange | furniture, interior, bathroom, storage | Bathroom cabinet |\n442:| `kenney-furniture/bathroom-cabinet-drawer` | 0.86 × 0.94 × 0.64 |  | wood sand, metalLight white, metalDark slate | furniture, interior, bathroom, storage | Bathroom cabinet drawer |\n443:| `kenney-furniture/bathroom-mirror` | 0.6 × 0.87 × 0.29 |  | wood sand, metal mist | furniture, interior, bathroom | Bathroom mirror |\n| id | size (m, w × h × d) | params: default (min–max) | palette slots | tags | about |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `kenney-furniture/bathroom-cabinet` | 0.46 × 0.78 × 0.26 |  | wood sand, metal mist, woodDark orange | furniture, interior, bathroom, storage | Bathroom cabinet |\n| `kenney-furniture/bathroom-cabinet-drawer` | 0.86 × 0.94 × 0.64 |  | wood sand, metalLight white, metalDark slate | furniture, interior, bathroom, storage | Bathroom cabinet drawer |\n| `kenney-furniture/bathroom-mirror` | 0.6 × 0.87 × 0.29 |  | wood sand, metal mist | furniture, interior, bathroom | Bathroom mirror |\n0 \n### loadPack()\n\n```ts\nfunction loadPack(url: string, opts: { readonly into?: ModelCatalog; readonly textures?: TextureCatalog } = {}): Promise<ModelCatalog>\n```\n\nLoad a pack of imported models and textures (`public/packs/<pack>.json`, docs/assets/importing.md\n*Packs*) once, the way `loadModel` loads a GLB: the URL resolved the same way (under the\nbase URL; a page may put a data URL for it in `__PIXEL_ASSETS__`, as single-file builds do for\nevery `packs/<id>.json` path the built code names, cut to the models it names), counted by\n`assetProgress`. Resolves to a catalog of the\npack's ModelDefs, to build from with `buildModel(id, { catalog })`; `into` also adds them to a\ncatalog of yours (e.g. `MODEL_LIBRARY`, so `use` finds them), and `textures` gets the pack's\nTextureDefs (e.g. `TEXTURE_LIBRARY`, so `textureMap(id)` and `hudSprite(id)` find them).\n\n### buildModel()\n\n```ts\nfunction buildModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: ModelOptions = {}): ModelBuild\n```\n\n### class Catalog\n\n- `new Catalog(defs: readonly T[] = [], kind = 'def', tool = '')`\n- `add(...defs: readonly T[]): this`: Add defs; an id that is already taken throws.\n- `has(id: string): boolean`\n- `get(id: string): T`\n- `all(): T[]`\n- `find(q: { tags?: readonly string[]; text?: string } = {}): T[]`: Defs with every tag in `tags` whose id, about or tags contain every word of `text`.\n- `search(text: string, o: SearchOptions = {}): T[]`: Defs ranked by how well they match `text`, best first (`searchDefs`).\n\n### interface CatalogEntry\n### compileClips()\n\n```ts\nfunction compileClips(defs: readonly ClipDef[], rig: RigSpec, model: Object3D): AnimationClip[]\n```\n\n### interface Foot\n\n- `readonly at: Vec3`: World position of the foot now.\n- `t: number`: Stepping: 0 → 1 through the step; -1 planted.\n- `readonly from: Vec3`\n- `readonly to: Vec3`\n\n### interface FootGoal\n\nFoot-placement IK: say where a foot should be, get the hip/knee/ankle rotations.\n### class Precipitation\n\n- `new Precipitation(o: PrecipitationOptions)`\n4598:### interface PrecipitationOptions\n4599-\n4600-- `kind: PrecipitationKind`\n4601-- `count: number`: Most drops at once (the instance count).\n4602-- `area?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Width, height and depth of the air the drops fall through, around the centre.\n4603-- `color?: number`: Drop colour (hex).\n4604-- `speed?: number`: Fall speed (m/s). Rain 16, snow 1.4.\n4605-\n4606-### interface Recording\n4607-\n4608-- `readonly format: 1`\n577:### class CameraRig\n578-\n579-Base rig: owns the three.js camera, zoom and the ground-plane movement basis.\n580-\n581-- `new CameraRig(config: CameraConfig)`\n582-- `readonly preset: CameraPreset`\n583-- `readonly camera: OrthographicCamera | PerspectiveCamera`\n584-- `readonly focus: Vector3`: World point the rig is centred on (used for shadow framing).\n585-- `zoom: number`\n586-- `readonly minZoom: number`\n587-- `readonly maxZoom: number`\n588-- `readonly zoomable: boolean`: Whether zoom applies (all presets except first person).\n589-- `readonly hidesTarget: boolean`: First person hides the player model.\n590-- `readonly lockDepth: boolean`: Side-scroller: characters should stay on their depth lane.\n591-- `controlsCharacter: boolean`: False while the free camera is flying (input drives the camera, not the player).\n592-- `snap: boolean`: Pixel-snap the camera (ortho only).\n593-- `aspect: number`: Viewport aspect (width / height), following the art resolution (see `setAspect`).\n594-- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane) and its unit direction. For picking things with the mouse, or aiming at it. An orthographic rig stands far b…\n595-- `setZoom(zoom: number): void`\n596-- `setAspect(aspect: number): void`: Match the art resolution's aspect (adaptive framing changes it with the screen). `update()` calls this from `CameraUpdate.resolution`; the engine also calls it on swap.\n597-- `teleport(target: Vector3): void`: Place the camera without smoothing.\n598-- `groundBasis(): { right: Vector3; forward: Vector3 }`: Screen-relative movement basis on the ground plane.\n599-- `update(u: CameraUpdate): void`\n600-- `describe(): Record<string, unknown>`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\n601-- `state(): CameraRigState`: The rig as data, exact (`engine.snapshot()`).\n602-- `setState(s: CameraRigState): void`: Put the rig back where `state()` found it (the same preset).\n603-","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"597d3a1c-db2a-4749-a8fd-5a8ff36f0d78","uuid":"d5d8cfce-fdd3-4188-a877-09ff48cfcc56","timestamp":"2026-11-05T15:39:57.979Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"435:### kenney-furniture: Kenney Furniture Kit 2.0\n437:140 models, 0 textures, CC0-1.0 by Kenney (https://kenney.nl/assets/furniture-kit). Load it: `const kit = await loadPack('packs/kenney-furniture.json')`, then `buildModel(id, { catalog: kit })`.\n441:| `kenney-furniture/bathroom-cabinet` | 0.46 × 0.78 × 0.26 |  | wood sand, metal mist, woodDark orange | furniture, interior, bathroom, storage | Bathroom cabinet |\n442:| `kenney-furniture/bathroom-cabinet-drawer` | 0.86 × 0.94 × 0.64 |  | wood sand, metalLight white, metalDark slate | furniture, interior, bathroom, storage | Bathroom cabinet drawer |\n443:| `kenney-furniture/bathroom-mirror` | 0.6 × 0.87 × 0.29 |  | wood sand, metal mist | furniture, interior, bathroom | Bathroom mirror |\n| id | size (m, w × h × d) | params: default (min–max) | palette slots | tags | about |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `kenney-furniture/bathroom-cabinet` | 0.46 × 0.78 × 0.26 |  | wood sand, metal mist, woodDark orange | furniture, interior, bathroom, storage | Bathroom cabinet |\n| `kenney-furniture/bathroom-cabinet-drawer` | 0.86 × 0.94 × 0.64 |  | wood sand, metalLight white, metalDark slate | furniture, interior, bathroom, storage | Bathroom cabinet drawer |\n| `kenney-furniture/bathroom-mirror` | 0.6 × 0.87 × 0.29 |  | wood sand, metal mist | furniture, interior, bathroom | Bathroom mirror |\n0 \n### loadPack()\n\n```ts\nfunction loadPack(url: string, opts: { readonly into?: ModelCatalog; readonly textures?: TextureCatalog } = {}): Promise<ModelCatalog>\n```\n\nLoad a pack of imported models and textures (`public/packs/<pack>.json`, docs/assets/importing.md\n*Packs*) once, the way `lo